      "name": "Cagrilintide + Tirzepatide Stack",
      "aliases": [],
      "kind": "other",
      "identityStatus": "needs_confirmation",
      "categoryID": 2,
      "benefits": "Proposed rationale based on separate components: subcutaneous cagrilintide and tirzepatide each produced weight reduction in human studies, so this pairing aims to combine their distinct appetite/metabolic actions for weight management. This is an inference from component evidence, not a demonstrated benefit of taking them together. No direct human combination benefit was verified; CagriSema trials and comparisons against tirzepatide do not validate this stack or an arbitrary mixture."
    }
