              "section": "Cagrilintide + Tirzepatide Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Common Community-Reported Side Effects",
              "excerpt": "Strong appetite suppression - usually a feature, sometimes uncomfortable.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Cagrilintide + Tirzepatide Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Common Community-Reported Side Effects",
              "excerpt": "Bloating or feeling overly full after small meals (delayed gastric emptying).",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Cagrilintide + Tirzepatide Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Contraindication Signals",
              "excerpt": "Standard conservative practice excludes anyone with active gastrointestinal disease, type 1 diabetes, prior pancreatitis, medullary thyroid carcinoma history, or active cancer from any tirzepatide protocol. Adding cagrilintide raises the GI tolerance bar further.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Cagrilintide + Tirzepatide Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "When to reassess",
              "excerpt": "If GI symptoms worsen instead of improving over the first 2-3 weeks of a step, if you cannot keep food down, or if you have severe persistent abdominal pain (especially with back radiation), pause and consult a qualified clinician. For broader stacking-safety context see the PepPal side-effects guide .",
              "truncated": false
            }
          ],
